<title>USA: AnnTaylor sees Q3 charge of $0.08 per share.</title>
<headline>AnnTaylor sees Q3 charge of $0.08 per share.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>AnnTaylor Stores Corp said on Thursday it expects to take a one-time charge in the third quarter of about $2 million, or $0.08 per share.</p>
<p>The charge reflects the company's contractual obligations to Sally Frame Kasaks, who resigned as chairman and chief executive on August 23, AnnTaylor said.</p>
